{"type":"proposed","id":"o1230050b80e5","subject":"module:agents","kind":"module-intent","claim":"26 single-purpose reference agents, one directory per agent, each a separate npm package with its own `bin`. 25 of the 26 import `sdk/typescript` for the protocol envelope (the exception is `agents/llm` itself, which the other 9 LLM-backed agents import for the tool loop: coder, planner, reviewer, pr-opener, issue-opener, issue-triage, policy-check, notion-worker, runtime); the rest are mechanical adapters over one vendor API. Each agent observes or acts on ONE task and emits protocol events — routing, retries, loop limits, durable state and webhooks are deliberately the orchestrator's, outside this repo. That boundary is why a per-agent claim says almost nothing: the interesting structure is the fleet, not the members.","by":"sol","at":"2026-08-12T00:53:44.789Z","citations":["agents/README.md:29"]}
